arguments.prompt:
You are implementing a shipment tracking Blazor Web App. The project has already been scaffolded at `/tmp/sv-cd943f8e64af4b8ea71ea103b4f56d1d/ShipmentTracker/` using `dotnet new blazor -int Auto -ai -au Individual`.

## Project Structure
- **Server project**: `/tmp/sv-cd943f8e64af4b8ea71ea103b4f56d1d/ShipmentTracker/ShipmentTracker/`
- **Client project**: `/tmp/sv-cd943f8e64af4b8ea71ea103b4f56d1d/ShipmentTracker/ShipmentTracker.Client/`
- Solution file: `/tmp/sv-cd943f8e64af4b8ea71ea103b4f56d1d/ShipmentTracker/ShipmentTracker.sln`

## Key Architecture Rules (Auto mode)
- **All interactive components go in the `.Client` project** — pages in `ShipmentTracker.Client/Pages/`.
- **No direct DB access from .Client** — components use service interfaces; client impl uses HttpClient, server impl uses EF Core.
- **Both Program.cs files must register matching services.**
- Global interactivity is already configured in App.razor — do NOT add `@rendermode` to pages.
- Identity/Account pages are static SSR — do NOT modify them.

## What to Implement

### 1. Shared Models (in `.Client` project)
Create `ShipmentTracker.Client/Models/ShipmentStatus.cs`:
```csharp
namespace ShipmentTracker.Client.Models;

public enum ShipmentStatus
{
    Pending,
    PickedUp,
    InTransit,
    OutForDelivery,
    Delivered,
    Cancelled
}
```

Create `ShipmentTracker.Client/Models/ShipmentDto.cs`:
```csharp
namespace ShipmentTracker.Client.Models;

public class ShipmentDto
{
    public int Id { get; set; }
    public string TrackingNumber { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public string Origin { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public string Destination { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public ShipmentStatus Status { get; set; }
    public DateTime ShippedDate { get; set; }
    public DateTime EstimatedDelivery { get; set; }
    public DateTime? ActualDelivery { get; set; }
    public string RecipientName { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public string Description { get; set; } = string.Empty;
}
```

### 2. Service Interface (in `.Client` project)
Create `ShipmentTracker.Client/Services/IShipmentService.cs`:
```csharp
namespace ShipmentTracker.Client.Services;

using ShipmentTracker.Client.Models;

public interface IShipmentService
{
    Task<List<ShipmentDto>> GetAllShipmentsAsync();
    Task<ShipmentDto?> GetByTrackingNumberAsync(string trackingNumber);
    Task<ShipmentDto?> UpdateStatusAsync(int id, ShipmentStatus newStatus);
}
```

### 3. Client-side Implementation (in `.Client` project)
Create `ShipmentTracker.Client/Services/ShipmentHttpService.cs` — implements `IShipmentService` using `HttpClient`:
```csharp
using System.Net.Http.Json;
using ShipmentTracker.Client.Models;

namespace ShipmentTracker.Client.Services;

public class ShipmentHttpService(HttpClient http) : IShipmentService
{
    public async Task<List<ShipmentDto>> GetAllShipmentsAsync()
    {
        return await http.GetFromJsonAsync<List<ShipmentDto>>("api/shipments") ?? [];
    }

    public async Task<ShipmentDto?> GetByTrackingNumberAsync(string trackingNumber)
    {
        var response = await http.GetAsync($"api/shipments/track/{Uri.EscapeDataString(trackingNumber)}");
        if (!response.IsSuccessStatusCode) return null;
        return await response.Content.ReadFromJsonAsync<ShipmentDto>();
    }

    public async Task<ShipmentDto?> UpdateStatusAsync(int id, ShipmentStatus newStatus)
    {
        var response = await http.PutAsJsonAsync($"api/shipments/{id}/status", newStatus);
        if (!response.IsSuccessStatusCode) return null;
        return await response.Content.ReadFromJsonAsync<ShipmentDto>();
    }
}
```

### 4. Server-side Data Model
Create `ShipmentTracker/Data/Shipment.cs`:
```csharp
namespace ShipmentTracker.Data;

public class Shipment
{
    public int Id { get; set; }
    public string TrackingNumber { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public string Origin { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public string Destination { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public int Status { get; set; } // maps to ShipmentStatus enum
    public DateTime ShippedDate { get; set; }
    public DateTime EstimatedDelivery { get; set; }
    public DateTime? ActualDelivery { get; set; }
    public string RecipientName { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public string Description { get; set; } = string.Empty;
}
```

Update `ApplicationDbContext` to add `DbSet<Shipment>`:
```csharp
using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Identity.EntityFrameworkCore;
using Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore;

